# No environment variables are required to run this app.
# All Supabase connection credentials are stored client-side in localStorage via Zustand persist.
# Add your connections directly in the app UI.

# For the Data Catalog AI feature, deploy the catalog-generator edge function to your Supabase
# project and set your OpenAI API key as a Supabase secret:
#   supabase functions deploy catalog-generator
#   supabase secrets set OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# ─── AI Agent (LLM) ───
# SELF-HOSTED / PRIVATE deployments only — do NOT set these on a public deployment.
# The proxy endpoint has no user authentication; anyone who can reach the site
# can consume your quota if a key is present.
#
# If left empty, users enter their own key in the agent settings panel (stored in
# their browser only — never sent to the server).
#
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-...
# Or provider-specific:
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=AIza...

# Optional: pre-fill Iceberg / S3 credentials for the Analytics tab.
# When set, these values auto-populate the S3 form fields (connection-stored values take priority).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_S3_WAREHOUSE=my-iceberg-bucket
# NEXT_PUBLIC_S3_KEY_ID=your-s3-access-key-id
# NEXT_PUBLIC_S3_SECRET=your-s3-secret-access-key
